; CARRY-1 (2026-09-19) — ROOM BOUNDS. The authored volume placement integrity layer 1 tests
; against (program doc §5b, a ruling from Talon): a prop may only be SET DOWN somewhere whose
; collision shape lies wholly inside one of these. It is the room's INTERIOR — floor top to
; ceiling underside, wall inner face to wall inner face — not the room's footprint, so a crate
; pushed half into a wall is outside it by construction.
;
; The GROUP is what PlacementIntegrity queries; the name is for whoever opens this scene looking
; for it. Groups go in the [node] header (.claude/rules/godot-scenes.md) — wired anywhere else
; they fail silently and look exactly like a feature that does nothing.
;
; It monitors nothing and is on no layer. It is a shape and a transform that the server reads
; directly; pairing it with every body that walks through it would be per-frame broadphase work
; for an answer nobody asks for.

[node name="RoomBounds" type="Area3D" parent="." groups=["room_bounds"]]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1.75, 0)
monitoring = false
monitorable = false
collision_layer = 0
collision_mask = 0

[node name="Collision" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="RoomBounds"]
shape = SubResource("BoxShape3D_bounds")

; CLOCK-1 (2026-09-19) — THE ROUND CLOCK. One instance of RoundClock.tscn, high on the -Z wall's
; inner face (the wall is at z = -5.2 and is 0.4 m thick, so its inner face is z = -5.0) looking
; at the centre of the room. Identity basis: a Label3D faces +Z with no rotation, which is into
; the room from this wall.
;
; y = 2.35 puts the panel's centre 1.31 m above the 1.04 m eyeline and its top 0.55 m clear of the
; ceiling, so it is looked UP at from anywhere in the room and is not something a body walks into
; -- it carries no collision at all (see RoundClock.tscn).
;
; WHICH ROOM THE CLOCK THINKS IT IS IN IS NOT AUTHORED HERE, and that is not an oversight.
; It was, on the first cut -- a `room = "..."` line on the instance below, against an [Export] on
; RoundClock -- and it read back EMPTY on all three clocks. Godot does not apply a nested
; PackedScene instance's exported C# script properties on this project's Godot/Mono build; the
; native properties on the same line (transform, mesh, mass) are unaffected, which is why this
; fails silently. PropManager.AuthoredKindOf and Carryable.LoadLiftM record the same trap from
; 2026-07 and 2026-09. RoundClock derives the room by walking up to THIS scene's root name, which
; is a native property and survives instancing.

[node name="RoundClock" parent="." instance=ExtResource("9_clock")]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 2.35, -4.94)


; BTN-1 (2026-09-19) — THE END ROUND BUTTON, on the +X wall beside the burst-door wall.
;
; BESIDE IT, NOT ON IT, and that is the packet's word taken literally for a reason. WallZPos is
; the wall DOOR-1 replaces with the burst door; a control mounted on the thing that is about to
; fly open would be a control that moves, and at the one moment both players are looking at it.
; This sits on the +X wall a metre and a half short of that corner, where the seeker walking in
; through the door and the hider standing at their tower can both reach it.
;
; MOUNTING: local +Z out of the wall — see HoldingRoom.tscn's StartButton header. This wall faces
; −X, so the basis is a quarter turn the other way and its twelve floats are (0,0,−1, 0,1,0,
; 1,0,0), written as basis ROWS (.claude/rules/godot-scenes.md). x = 4.94 is the wall's inner
; face (5.0) minus the plate's half-depth.
;
; EITHER PLAYER MAY PRESS IT (IRoundFactSource.AnyPressedEnd, verbatim): the beat after the
; startle belongs to both of them, and whoever has had enough of it ends it.

[node name="EndButton" type="StaticBody3D" parent="." groups=["pressable", "round_button", "round_button_end"]]
transform = Transform3D(0, 0, -1, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0, 4.94, 1.15, 3.6)
script = ExtResource("1_button")

