; TASK-1 (2026-09-19) -- THE SORTING JOB. Everything below is the hider job: a supply crate of
; eighteen sortables, three bins along the +Z wall, and one poll node.
;
; THE RULE OF THE ROUND IS NOT AUTHORED HERE AND MUST NOT BE. SortRule.For(round) is odd -> sort
; by COLOUR, even -> sort by SHAPE, derived on every peer from the round index the wire already
; carries. Nothing in this file says which round is which, so the level cannot disagree with the
; loop about what the bins are asking for.
;
; NEITHER OF A SORTABLE TWO FACTS IS AN [Export], AND BOTH LIVE IN NATIVE PROPERTIES.
;   COLOUR is the suffix of the NetworkedProp node name -- Sort_000_Red. A node name survives
;          instancing; an exported C# script property on a node inside an instanced sub-scene does
;          NOT on this Godot/Mono build, and TaskRoom.tscn is instanced into Supermarket.tscn.
;          That trap has now been paid for four times: PropManager.AuthoredKindOf (Crate.tscn
;          kind/tint, 2026-07), Carryable.LoadLiftM, RoundClock.Room (CLOCK-1 3.1) and
;          BurstDoor room-light lookup (CARRY-1 section 6).
;   SHAPE  is the Body COLLIDER, through Carryable.ShapeFromCollider -- the same table that
;          decides the prop wire kind and its SFX-1 material, so the sound and the sort can
;          never disagree about what an object is. Cube -> cubic box -> Crate -> Wood;
;          ball -> 0.08 m sphere -> Produce; can -> cylinder -> Can -> Tin. The three therefore
;          also SOUND different, which is the packet own reason for choosing these shapes.
;
; THE NUMBERING IS THE ID ORDER. PropManager.AdoptAuthoredProps sorts by NODE PATH, and
; "SearchRoom" sorts before "TaskRoom", so SearchRoom.tscn four crates keep ids 1000-1003 and
; these eighteen are 1004-1021 in the order written below. Renaming or reordering one renumbers
; the rest; tests/Run-SortTest.ps1 names ids, so it would notice.
;
; STRUCTURE, and it is not optional: a NetworkedProp (Node3D + script) whose child is literally
; named "Body" and instances one of the three prefabs, plus a SortItem child. NetworkedProp._Ready
; binds the Body rather than building one.
;
; THE CRATE IS NOT PRE-SORTED. The eighteen are interleaved on the 6 x 3 grid so no row and no
; column is a group under either rule -- a crate that arrived already sorted by colour would hand
; the player the answer to round 1 and make round 2 read as a trick.
;
; WHERE THINGS ARE. The crate is at (-2, 0, 1) and the bins are at x = 1.2 / 2.0 / 2.8, z = 4.6 --
; about 5 m apart, so a trip is a real walk and being found mid-carry is the ordinary case rather
; than bad luck. The bins are all inside DOOR-1 BurstRadiusM (3.0 m from the doorway at
; (0, 1.1, 5.2)): measured from an object resting in one, 1.39 m / 2.12 m / 2.89 m. The crate is
; about 7 m away and outside it on purpose -- the burst disturbs the WORK, not the supply.
; The bins sit to the +X side of the doorway, clear of the leaf swing (which reaches x = -1.33).
;
; All twelve floats of every Transform3D below are basis ROWS (.claude/rules/godot-scenes.md);
; every one is the identity basis plus a translation.

